# i18n UI Copy

All user-facing strings on classclarus-web must use `useTranslation` / `Trans` from `react-i18next`, not hardcoded text.

## Adding copy

1. Add the key to `i18n/resources/en.ts` first (source of truth).
2. Mirror the key in every locale file: `de`, `es`, `fr`, `it`, `ja`, `ko`, `nl`, `pt`, `ru`, `th`, `uk`, `zhs`, `zht`.
3. `engb` reuses the English catalog — do not add `engb.ts`.
4. Run `bun test` — `i18n/catalog.test.ts` enforces key parity across locales.

## Namespaces

Use feature namespaces (`hero`, `pricing`, `faq`, etc.) or `common` for shared chrome. Keep each namespace flat (`Record<string, string>`).

## Language preference

Matches classclarus-app: `classclarus-language` in localStorage plus a `classclarus-language` cookie on `.classclarus.com` so the marketing site and app share the same preference across subdomains. No locale-prefixed routes.
